  8. Business Mutation Metrics — Committed-Only Semantics

  The DESIGN.md requires measuring committed Area Mutations. http.server.requests counts requests that return 400, 409, 429, and 500 alongside successful 200/201 responses. Counting these as "mutations" would be incorrect.

  Proposed mechanism: A new AreaMetricsListener component listens to AreaEventMessage via @TransactionalEventListener(phase = TransactionPhase.AFTER_COMMIT). This is the same event already published by AreaService and already consumed by AreaEventRelay. Adding a second @TransactionalEventListener for the same event type is supported — Spring fires all listeners. This guarantees the counter is incremented only after the DB transaction commits, identical semantics to the WebSocket event.

  Counter: area.mutations.committed.total with tag change_type ∈ {CREATED, UPDATED, DELETED, RESTORED}.

  No changes to AreaService are needed.

