  11. WebSocket Metrics Decision

  Active connection count: Implementable via a ChannelInterceptor that intercepts StompCommand.CONNECTED and StompCommand.DISCONNECT/ERROR. This would be a new MetricsChannelInterceptor registered alongside JwtChannelInterceptor in WebSocketConfig.configureClientInboundChannel().

  Event propagation latency: Not measurable from a single JVM. The path is: AreaService.eventPublisher → AreaEventRelay.onAreaEvent → SimpMessagingTemplate.convertAndSend → STOMP broker → WebSocket delivery to client. The end-to-end latency (the SLO p95 < 200 ms) includes the STOMP broker delivery and network; it cannot be measured by the sender. Decision: document as a production limitation.

  WebSocket reconnect rate: Client-side signal. The backend sees a new CONNECT after a reconnect but cannot distinguish a reconnect from a first connect. Decision: not measurable; document as limitation.

