  16. Transaction / Commit Semantics

  The area.mutations.committed.total counter must be incremented only after a successful DB commit. Using @TransactionalEventListener(phase = AFTER_COMMIT) on AreaEventMessage provides exactly this guarantee — the same semantic already used by AreaEventRelay.

  A direct counter increment inside AreaService.@Transactional methods would be wrong: the counter increments before commit, so a transaction rollback (due to a constraint violation) would still increment the counter. The AFTER_COMMIT listener pattern is the correct mechanism.

  VERSION_CONFLICT and rate limit rejection counters are correctly placed outside any transaction (in GlobalExceptionHandler and DrawingRateLimitInterceptor respectively) because those code paths confirm that no transaction was committed or it was rolled back.

